  "notes": [
    "KPA-39 on real fixture (1 m, Quail Island): 127 order-1 links at 0.20 ha; 126 refused, of which 0 were refused by the prominence test. find_keypoints reports all 126 as 'no break in the floor clearing 2% of grade change', so the stated reason is false 126/126 times. Breakdown: 78x :674 (thalweg is None or len(thalweg) < 5), 48x :722 (n_samp - 2*guard < 3 \u2014 profile too short to have an interior)",
    "KPA-43 on real fixture (1 m, Quail Island): at max_valleys=1, keypoints+skipped = 3 against 127 links (124 links never examined and never reported); at max_valleys=8, 127 against 127 (0 unaccounted).",
    "KPA-40 on real fixture (1 m): the shortest axis-aligned thalweg that can yield a keypoint is 36 cells = 35.0 m (predicted floor 7 x min(5*cell, 10) = 35 m). Every shorter link is still emitted by stream_links and still profiled.",
    "KPA-41, measured: the steepest 20 m window on ridge_guide at offset 15.0 m runs 1:6.3, while _run_record reports its net drift as 1:544.8 and over_limit False. Understatement factor 86.4x.",
    "KPA-42, measured: 3 of 7 guides carry vertices whose Z is _sample_dem's default (the keypoint elevation) rather than sampled ground \u2014 valley_guide@-5.0m: 9/151; valley_guide@-10.0m: 19/146; valley_guide@-15.0m: 27/143. A guide whose net fall is computed between two fabricated ends reports a drift that is an artefact of the default, not of terrain.",
    "KPA-39 on default harness DEM (2 m, 36 ha): 28 order-1 links at 0.20 ha; 28 refused, of which 26 were refused by the prominence test. find_keypoints reports all 28 as 'no break in the floor clearing 2% of grade change', so the stated reason is false 2/28 times. Breakdown: 2x :722 (n_samp - 2*guard < 3 \u2014 profile too short to have an interior), 26x :734 (slope_ease < MIN_SLOPE_EASE \u2014 the prominence test)",
    "KPA-43 on default harness DEM (2 m, 36 ha): at max_valleys=1, keypoints+skipped = 28 against 28 links (0 links never examined and never reported); at max_valleys=8, 28 against 28 (0 unaccounted).",
    "KPA-40 on default harness DEM (2 m): the shortest axis-aligned thalweg that can yield a keypoint is 36 cells = 70.0 m (predicted floor 7 x min(5*cell, 10) = 70 m). Every shorter link is still emitted by stream_links and still profiled.",
    "Window sizing (a TerrainFlow convention, sized on SYNTHETIC correlated roughness \u2014 no published source supplies one): spreads across roughness_m 0.00-0.10 on the trunk keyline are 10m 0.0435 (2.18x MIN_SLOPE_EASE); 20m 0.0488 (2.44x MIN_SLOPE_EASE); 50m 0.0165 (0.82x MIN_SLOPE_EASE). Shortest window whose spread stays under MIN_SLOPE_EASE: 50m.",
    "The sweep's own result contradicts the hypothesis it was written to test. Correlated roughness does NOT push slope_ease over MIN_SLOPE_EASE spuriously \u2014 it does the opposite. As roughness_m goes 0.00 -> 0.25 the order-1 link count rises 28 -> 263 -> 327 -> 356 while the links that are long enough to profile at all fall 26 -> 3 -> 1 -> 0, and the number clearing the 2% bar stays 0 throughout. Noise shatters the channel network into stubs that FLG-18's floor then refuses, so the failure mode is KPA-39's length guards, not a false positive on prominence."
  ],
